From bbfc6708254b3bdb248134ef0ddacefd805e8303 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Campos Ramos <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>
Date: Tue, 22 Sep 2026 15:36:27 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] nvidia-modeset: raise default max_output_color_depth to
 12

NVKMS already parses the sink's HDMI Deep Color capability (VSDB
DC_30/DC_36/DC_48) and already constructs and programs 10/12-bpc output
for RGB and YCbCr 4:4:4, 4:2:2 and 4:2:0.  The only piece keeping a
12-bpc-capable sink at 10 bpc on Linux is this module parameter's
default.  Windows on the same hardware drives the same sink at 12 bpc.

Measured narrowing, GA106 + Sony KDL-46HX855 (EDID declares
DC_30/DC_36): Linux 615.71.09 selects 10 bpc where amdgpu on the same
sink selects 12 bpc.  Refs NVIDIA/open-gpu-kernel-modules#1384.

The module parameter still permits capping at 10; this only lifts the
default so the EDID-declared capability is what decides.

Signed-off-by: Daniel Campos Ramos <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>
Co-Authored-By: Kimi K3 (Claude Code) <noreply@anthropic.com>
Co-Authored-By: OpenAI Codex <noreply@openai.com>
---
 kernel-open/nvidia-modeset/nvidia-modeset-linux.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/kernel-open/nvidia-modeset/nvidia-modeset-linux.c b/kernel-open/nvidia-modeset/nvidia-modeset-linux.c
index 62986c4..9c0ae49 100644
--- a/kernel-open/nvidia-modeset/nvidia-modeset-linux.c
+++ b/kernel-open/nvidia-modeset/nvidia-modeset-linux.c
@@ -92,7 +92,7 @@ module_param_named(disable_vrr_memclk_switch, disable_vrr_memclk_switch, bool, 0
 static bool hdmi_deepcolor = true;
 module_param_named(hdmi_deepcolor, hdmi_deepcolor, bool, 0444);
 
-static unsigned int max_output_color_depth = 10;
+static unsigned int max_output_color_depth = 12;
 module_param_named(max_output_color_depth, max_output_color_depth, uint, 0444);
 
 static bool opportunistic_display_sync = true;
-- 
2.53.0

